{"type":"text","timestamp":1789824788570,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"id":"prt_0b9dec9b5001YjpTZrBMWAeTTD","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9de09bf001w3cFlyf6UUT28O","type":"text","text":"Let me verify the exact quotations I plan to use against the filing text.","time":{"start":1789824780725,"end":1789824788570}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789824788607,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9deca03001NRhJN3w8lyRSTn","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9de09bf001w3cFlyf6UUT28O","type":"tool","id":"call_00_uO6EEWVBttRK2QZnbGZo7592","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\ntext = open('filing_text.txt').read()\nquotes = [\n\"In March, 2014, the board authorized management to contact Industry Participant to determine Industry Participant\\u2019s interest in initiating exploratory discussions concerning the feasibility of a merger or acquisition transaction.\",\n\"During the Spring of 2014, David Lenhardt, PetSmart\\u2019s chief executive officer, spoke on a few occasions to Industry Participant\\u2019s CEO.\",\n\"Industry Participant\\u2019s CEO informed Mr. Lenhardt that Industry Participant was not for sale\",\n\"determined to explore more intensively potential changes to the Company\\u2019s capital structure, with a focus on returning capital to stockholders.\",\n\"The board also established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee\",\n\"the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (\\u201cWachtell Lipton\\u201d), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives\",\n\"In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor\",\n\"Pursuant to an engagement letter effective as of August 21, 2014, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as its financial advisor\",\n\"For services rendered in connection with the merger and the delivery of its opinion, the Company has agreed to pay J.P. Morgan an amount up to approximately $39 million\",\n\"On July 3, 2014, JANA Partners filed a Schedule 13D with the SEC disclosing that JANA had acquired 9.9% of the Company\\u2019s outstanding common stock\",\n\"Longview would consider, depending on the parties and terms involved, rolling part or all of its holdings into equity of the acquiring entity rather than receive cash consideration\",\n\"Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the conversations that had taken place in the Spring concerning the feasibility of a possible combination of the two Companies\",\n\"determined to explore strategic alternatives (including a possible sale of the Company) for the Company to maximize value for stockholders\",\n\"the Company issued a press release announcing that it determined to explore strategic alternatives for the Company to maximize value for stockholders, including a possible sale of the Company\",\n\"The J.P. Morgan representative stated that Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process, but that if Industry Participant were to wish to submit a proposal or other communication to the Company, the board would consider it.\",\n\"J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants in a sale process, including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants\",\n\"the board was informed that approximately 15 parties had expressed interest in participating in the process\",\n\"reaffirmed the determination not to invite Industry Participant to participate in the sale process\",\n\"In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers\",\n\"all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management presentations involving the Company\\u2019s senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business plan information\",\n\"non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014\",\n\"willing to \\u201croll-over\\u201d up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview\",\n\"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest.\",\n\"the Buyer Group, which indicated a range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share\",\n\"another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share\",\n\"Bidder 2, which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\",\n\"Three bidders initially indicated price ranges that reached at least $80.00 per share\",\n\"increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share\",\n\"the board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process\",\n\"representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at price levels above their respective initial indications\",\n\"After deliberation and consultation with the Company\\u2019s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together.\",\n\"We refer to these two bidders together as \\u201cBidder 3.\\u201d\",\n\"the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids\",\n\"had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids\",\n\"Following the Company\\u2019s third quarter earnings announcement and, at the request of bidders and the direction of the board and the Company, representatives of J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the Company\\u2019s fiscal year 2014 financial projections.\",\n\"the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time, which would reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure.\",\n\"Accordingly, the Company set the evening of Wednesday, December 10\",\n\"On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.\",\n\"The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash, and Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash.\",\n\"The form of merger agreement and other transaction documentation submitted by the Buyer Group were more favorable to the Company\",\n\"each bidder indicated that its bid was not dependent on a rollover by Longview\",\n\"Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share.\",\n\"J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.\",\n\"the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014.\",\n\"each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents\",\n\"Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.\",\n\"Longview\\u2019s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.\",\n\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.\",\n\"Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\",\n\"the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group\\u2019s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price\",\n\"the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders\",\n\"subject, however, to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved\",\n\"On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\",\n\"as of February 2, 2015, the date of this proxy statement, no person has made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart\",\n\"neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group\",\n\"Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (\\u201crollover shares\\u201d) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent\",\n\"Longview will receive the same $83.00 per share merger consideration as the other holders of the Company\\u2019s common stock for all other shares of common stock beneficially owned by it (other than the rollover shares).\",\n\"the \\u201cBuyer Group\\u201d refers to a consortium of funds advised by BC Partners, Inc., La Caisse de d\\u00e9p\\u00f4t et placement du Qu\\u00e9bec, affiliates of GIC Special Investments Pte Ltd, affiliates of StepStone Group LP and, at all times after December 12, 2014, Longview Asset Management, LLC\",\n\"Each share of common stock outstanding at the effective time of the merger\",\n\"$83.00 in cash\",\n\"Argos Holdings Inc. is a Delaware corporation.\",\n\"PetSmart, Inc. is a Delaware corporation with principal executive offices located at 19601 North 27th Avenue, Phoenix, Arizona 85027.\",\n\"a premium of 38.8% to the Company\\u2019s stock price on July 2, 2014\",\n\"received first round indications of interest from 5 bidder groups\",\n\"entered into non-disclosure agreements with and engaged in due diligence or provided management presentation to 15 potential bidders\",\n\"the confidentiality agreements entered into by the 15 potentially interested parties that engaged in due diligence contained standstill provisions that prevent those parties from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once the Company entered into a definitive transaction agreement with the winning sale process participant\",\n\"The fact that Longview, which as of the date of the merger agreement managed 9% of the Company\\u2019s outstanding stock, and which is a long-term investor in the Company, supports and has agreed to vote in favor of the merger.\",\n\"The closing sale price of our common stock on December 12, 2014, which was the last trading day before the merger was publicly announced, was $77.67 per share.\",\n\"there were 99,455,151 shares of common stock outstanding\",\n\"This proxy statement is dated February 2, 2015 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about February 2, 2015.\",\n\"On December 14, 2014, members of the Buyer Group (other than Longview) entered into equity commitment letters\",\n\"up to $1.83 billion in cash in the aggregate\",\n\"Longview\\u2019s contribution to Parent of $250 million worth of the Company\\u2019s common stock\",\n\"up to approximately $6.2 billion as well as a $750 million senior secured asset-backed revolving credit facility\",\n\"approximately $425 million of cash is expected to be on hand\",\n\"In connection with the entry into the merger agreement, Merger Sub has (i) obtained a commitment letter\",\n\"Citigroup Global Markets Inc., Barclays Bank PLC, Deutsche Bank AG New York Branch, Nomura Securities International, Inc. and Jefferies Finance LLC\",\n\"RBC Capital Markets, Macquarie Capital (USA) Inc. and Natixis, New York Branch\",\n\"to pay to the Company a reverse termination fee of $510 million\",\n\"the Company must pay a termination fee of $255 million\",\n\"Innisfree M&A Incorporated, a proxy solicitation firm, has been retained to assist it in the solicitation of proxies\",\n\"JANA Partners LLC (3)  \\u200b 5,050,107\",\n\"Longview Asset Management, LLC (1)  \\u200b 8,214,170\",\n\"Vanguard Group, Inc (2)  \\u200b 7,404,716\",\n]\nmissing = [q for q in quotes if q not in text]\nprint(\"total\", len(quotes), \"missing\", len(missing))\nfor m in missing: print(\"MISSING:\", m[:100])\nEOF"},"output":"total 84 missing 11\nMISSING: Bidder 2, which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\nMISSING: the board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.0\nMISSING: the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time,\nMISSING: each bidder indicated that its bid was not dependent on a rollover by Longview\nMISSING: the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group’s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer\nMISSING: Each share of common stock outstanding at the effective time of the merger\nMISSING: up to approximately $6.2 billion as well as a $750 million senior secured asset-backed revolving cre\nMISSING: to pay to the Company a reverse termination fee of $510 million\nMISSING: JANA Partners LLC (3)  ​ 5,050,107\nMISSING: Longview Asset Management, LLC (1)  ​ 8,214,170\nMISSING: Vanguard Group, Inc (2)  ​ 7,404,716\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 84 missing 11\nMISSING: Bidder 2, which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\nMISSING: the board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.0\nMISSING: the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time,\nMISSING: each bidder indicated that its bid was not dependent on a rollover by Longview\nMISSING: the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group’s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer\nMISSING: Each share of common stock outstanding at the effective time of the merger\nMISSING: up to approximately $6.2 billion as well as a $750 million senior secured asset-backed revolving cre\nMISSING: to pay to the Company a reverse termination fee of $510 million\nMISSING: JANA Partners LLC (3)  ​ 5,050,107\nMISSING: Longview Asset Management, LLC (1)  ​ 8,214,170\nMISSING: Vanguard Group, Inc (2)  ​ 7,404,716\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\\ntext = open('filing_text.txt').read()\\nquotes = [\\n\\\"In March, 2014, the board authorized management to contact Industry Participant to determine Industry Participant\\\\u2019s interest in initiating exploratory discussions concerning the feasibility of a merger or acquisition transaction.\\\",\\n\\\"During the Spring of 2014, David Lenhardt, PetSmart\\\\u2019s chief executive officer, spoke on a few occasions to Industry Participant\\\\u2019s CEO.\\\",\\n\\\"Industry Participant\\\\u2019s CEO informed Mr. Lenhardt that Industry Participant was not for sale\\\",\\n\\\"determined to explore more intensively potential changes to the Company\\\\u2019s capital structure, with a focus on returning capital to stockholders.\\\",\\n\\\"The board also established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee\\\",\\n\\\"the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (\\\\u201cWachtell Lipton\\\\u201d), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives\\\",\\n\\\"In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor\\\",\\n\\\"Pursuant to an engagement letter effective as of August 21, 2014, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as its financial advisor\\\",\\n\\\"For services rendered in connection with the merger and the delivery of its opinion, the Company has agreed to pay J.P. Morgan an amount up to approximately $39 million\\\",\\n\\\"On July 3, 2014, JANA Partners filed a Schedule 13D with the SEC disclosing that JANA had acquired 9.9% of the Company\\\\u2019s outstanding common stock\\\",\\n\\\"Longview would consider, depending on the parties and terms involved, rolling part or all of its holdings into equity of the acquiring entity rather than receive cash consideration\\\",\\n\\\"Industry Participant might be interested in re-visiting the conversations that had taken place in the Spring concerning the feasibility of a possible combination of the two Companies\\\",\\n\\\"determined to explore strategic alternatives (including a possible sale of the Company) for the Company to maximize value for stockholders\\\",\\n\\\"the Company issued a press release announcing that it determined to explore strategic alternatives for the Company to maximize value for stockholders, including a possible sale of the Company\\\",\\n\\\"The J.P. Morgan representative stated that Industry Participant would not be invited into the exploratory process, but that if Industry Participant were to wish to submit a proposal or other communication to the Company, the board would consider it.\\\",\\n\\\"J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants in a sale process, including three strategic parties (not counting Industry Participant) and 24 financial participants\\\",\\n\\\"the board was informed that approximately 15 parties had expressed interest in participating in the process\\\",\\n\\\"reaffirmed the determination not to invite Industry Participant to participate in the sale process\\\",\\n\\\"In the first week of October 2014, the Company entered into confidentiality and standstill agreements with 15 potentially interested financial buyers\\\",\\n\\\"all 15 of which, during the month of October engaged in due diligence, received management presentations involving the Company\\\\u2019s senior-most management, and received detailed financial and business plan information\\\",\\n\\\"non-binding preliminary indications of interest would be due on October 30, 2014\\\",\\n\\\"willing to \\\\u201croll-over\\\\u201d up to 7.5 million shares on terms and price acceptable to Longview\\\",\\n\\\"On October 30, six of the potentially interested parties submitted indications of interest.\\\",\\n\\\"the Buyer Group, which indicated a range of $81.00 to $83.00 per share\\\",\\n\\\"another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share\\\",\\n\\\"Bidder 2, which had initially indicated a price of $78.00\\\",\\n\\\"Three bidders initially indicated price ranges that reached at least $80.00 per share\\\",\\n\\\"increased its indication to a range of $81.00 to $84.00 per share\\\",\\n\\\"the board determined to allow the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round of the sale process\\\",\\n\\\"representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at price levels above their respective initial indications\\\",\\n\\\"After deliberation and consultation with the Company\\\\u2019s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together.\\\",\\n\\\"We refer to these two bidders together as \\\\u201cBidder 3.\\\\u201d\\\",\\n\\\"the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids\\\",\\n\\\"had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids\\\",\\n\\\"Following the Company\\\\u2019s third quarter earnings announcement and, at the request of bidders and the direction of the board and the Company, representatives of J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the Company\\\\u2019s fiscal year 2014 financial projections.\\\",\\n\\\"the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time, which would reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure.\\\",\\n\\\"Accordingly, the Company set the evening of Wednesday, December 10\\\",\\n\\\"On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.\\\",\\n\\\"The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash, and Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash.\\\",\\n\\\"The form of merger agreement and other transaction documentation submitted by the Buyer Group were more favorable to the Company\\\",\\n\\\"each bidder indicated that its bid was not dependent on a rollover by Longview\\\",\\n\\\"Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share.\\\",\\n\\\"J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.\\\",\\n\\\"the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014.\\\",\\n\\\"each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents\\\",\\n\\\"Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.\\\",\\n\\\"Longview\\\\u2019s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.\\\",\\n\\\"During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.\\\",\\n\\\"Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.\\\",\\n\\\"the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group\\\\u2019s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price\\\",\\n\\\"the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders\\\",\\n\\\"subject, however, to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved\\\",\\n\\\"On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.\\\",\\n\\\"as of February 2, 2015, the date of this proxy statement, no person has made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart\\\",\\n\\\"neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group\\\",\\n\\\"Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (\\\\u201crollover shares\\\\u201d) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent\\\",\\n\\\"Longview will receive the same $83.00 per share merger consideration as the other holders of the Company\\\\u2019s common stock for all other shares of common stock beneficially owned by it (other than the rollover shares).\\\",\\n\\\"the \\\\u201cBuyer Group\\\\u201d refers to a consortium of funds advised by BC Partners, Inc., La Caisse de d\\\\u00e9p\\\\u00f4t et placement du Qu\\\\u00e9bec, affiliates of GIC Special Investments Pte Ltd, affiliates of StepStone Group LP and, at all times after December 12, 2014, Longview Asset Management, LLC\\\",\\n\\\"Each share of common stock outstanding at the effective time of the merger\\\",\\n\\\"$83.00 in cash\\\",\\n\\\"Argos Holdings Inc. is a Delaware corporation.\\\",\\n\\\"PetSmart, Inc. is a Delaware corporation with principal executive offices located at 19601 North 27th Avenue, Phoenix, Arizona 85027.\\\",\\n\\\"a premium of 38.8% to the Company\\\\u2019s stock price on July 2, 2014\\\",\\n\\\"received first round indications of interest from 5 bidder groups\\\",\\n\\\"entered into non-disclosure agreements with and engaged in due diligence or provided management presentation to 15 potential bidders\\\",\\n\\\"the confidentiality agreements entered into by the 15 potentially interested parties that engaged in due diligence contained standstill provisions that prevent those parties from submitting (or even seeking permission to submit) a higher bid once the Company entered into a definitive transaction agreement with the winning sale process participant\\\",\\n\\\"The fact that Longview, which as of the date of the merger agreement managed 9% of the Company\\\\u2019s outstanding stock, and which is a long-term investor in the Company, supports and has agreed to vote in favor of the merger.\\\",\\n\\\"The closing sale price of our common stock on December 12, 2014, which was the last trading day before the merger was publicly announced, was $77.67 per share.\\\",\\n\\\"there were 99,455,151 shares of common stock outstanding\\\",\\n\\\"This proxy statement is dated February 2, 2015 and is first being mailed to stockholders on or about February 2, 2015.\\\",\\n\\\"On December 14, 2014, members of the Buyer Group (other than Longview) entered into equity commitment letters\\\",\\n\\\"up to $1.83 billion in cash in the aggregate\\\",\\n\\\"Longview\\\\u2019s contribution to Parent of $250 million worth of the Company\\\\u2019s common stock\\\",\\n\\\"up to approximately $6.2 billion as well as a $750 million senior secured asset-backed revolving credit facility\\\",\\n\\\"approximately $425 million of cash is expected to be on hand\\\",\\n\\\"In connection with the entry into the merger agreement, Merger Sub has (i) obtained a commitment letter\\\",\\n\\\"Citigroup Global Markets Inc., Barclays Bank PLC, Deutsche Bank AG New York Branch, Nomura Securities International, Inc. and Jefferies Finance LLC\\\",\\n\\\"RBC Capital Markets, Macquarie Capital (USA) Inc. and Natixis, New York Branch\\\",\\n\\\"to pay to the Company a reverse termination fee of $510 million\\\",\\n\\\"the Company must pay a termination fee of $255 million\\\",\\n\\\"Innisfree M&A Incorporated, a proxy solicitation firm, has been retained to assist it in the solicitation of proxies\\\",\\n\\\"JANA Partners LLC (3)  \\\\u200b 5,050,107\\\",\\n\\\"Longview Asset Management, LLC (1)  \\\\u200b 8,214,170\\\",\\n\\\"Vanguard Group, Inc (2)  \\\\u200b 7,404,716\\\",\\n]\\nmissing = [q for q in quotes if q not in text]\\nprint(\\\"total\\\", len(quotes), \\\"missing\\\", len(missing))\\nfor m in missing: print(\\\"MISSING:\\\", m[:100])\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789824780803,"end":1789824788607}}}}
