{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825127845,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e4150b001oampFAMQHUg4wn","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9e40d2a001o8q6W85TG2VYWd","type":"tool","id":"call_00_ET_IncOjjKhHK7ui3jOmyEG8861","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_dump.txt","limit":180},"output":"Read file /tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_dump.txt, lines 1-180\n1: ### 1 R001 | When: March 2014 (discussions during Spring 2014) | Who: PetSmart (management) / Industry Participant (a privately held industry participant) | What: Target interest | P1 R0 | Type: None\n2: TERMS: Board authorized management in March 2014 to approach Industry Participant about a possible merger with or acquisition of it; CEO David Lenhardt spoke with Industry Participant's CEO over the Spring. Industry Participant said it was not for sale and believed antitrust clearance would not be obtained, or only with unacceptable conditions. PetSmart's own acquisition attempt, not a bid in its sale process; kept as context for the later decision to exclude Industry Participant.\n3: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n4: WHY: Stated: the board used the first quarter of 2014 to consider an acquisition of another industry participant; direction is target-to-Industry Participant. “In March, 2014, the board authorized management to contact Industry Participant to determine Industry Participant’s interest in initiating exploratory discussions concerning the feasibility of a merger or acquisition transaction.” “Industry Participant’s CEO informed Mr. Lenhardt that Industry Participant was not for sale”. Scope is the whole of Industry Participant, not a bid for PetSmart.\n5: SRC: P-001 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R007; R010\n6: DATES: 2014-03-01 00:00:00 -> 2014-05-31 00:00:00 WD 2014-03-01 00:00:00 (Reported interval / Assigned: bound) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n7: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n8: \n9: ### 2 R002 | When: 06/18/2014 | Who: PetSmart board | What: Target decision | P1 R0 | Type: None\n10: TERMS: Board reviewed strategic and financial alternatives with a financial adviser and Wachtell Lipton; determined to explore capital-structure changes intensively, focused on returning capital to stockholders; established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee of independent directors (Gregory Josefowicz, Rakesh Gangwal, Thomas Stemberg) and authorized vetting and retention of a financial adviser. No sale decision at this meeting. R1 anchor candidate, rejected (R013).\n11: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n12: WHY: Stated: June 18, 2014 board review and governance steps; a capital-structure review, not yet a sale decision. “At a meeting on June 18, 2014, the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives potentially available to the Company”. Follows the 05/21/2014 weak Q1 release and late-May/June communications from stockholders and interested parties.\n13: SRC: P-002; P-003 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R004; R008\n14: DATES: 2014-06-18 00:00:00 -> 2014-06-18 00:00:00 WD 2014-06-18 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n15: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n16: \n17: ### 3 R003 | When: 06/18/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz | What: Adviser service observed | P1 R0 | Type: None\n18: TERMS: Legal adviser to PetSmart, described as its legal advisor and shown acting at the June 18, 2014 board meeting and throughout the process (negotiations, merger agreement, voting agreement). Engagement date not disclosed; observed service treated as the mandate start.\n19: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | 