ant said it was not for sale and believed antitrust clearance would not be obtained, or only with unacceptable conditions. PetSmart's own acquisition attempt, not a bid in its sale process; kept as context for the later decision to exclude Industry Participant.\n3: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n4: WHY: Stated: the board used the first quarter of 2014 to consider an acquisition of another industry participant; direction is target-to-Industry Participant. “In March, 2014, the board authorized management to contact Industry Participant to determine Industry Participant’s interest in initiating exploratory discussions concerning the feasibility of a merger or acquisition transaction.” “Industry Participant’s CEO informed Mr. Lenhardt that Industry Participant was not for sale”. Scope is the whole of Industry Participant, not a bid for PetSmart.\n5: SRC: P-001 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R007; R010\n6: DATES: 2014-03-01 00:00:00 -> 2014-05-31 00:00:00 WD 2014-03-01 00:00:00 (Reported interval / Assigned: bound) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n7: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n8: \n9: ### 2 R002 | When: 06/18/2014 | Who: PetSmart board | What: Target decision | P1 R0 | Type: None\n10: TERMS: Board reviewed strategic and financial alternatives with a financial adviser and Wachtell Lipton; determined to explore capital-structure changes intensively, focused on returning capital to stockholders; established an ad hoc advisory subcommittee of independent directors (Gregory Josefowicz, Rakesh Gangwal, Thomas Stemberg) and authorized vetting and retention of a financial adviser. No sale decision at this meeting. R1 anchor candidate, rejected (R013).\n11: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n12: WHY: Stated: June 18, 2014 board review and governance steps; a capital-structure review, not yet a sale decision. “At a meeting on June 18, 2014, the board reviewed, together with a financial advisor and with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor, the various strategic and financial alternatives potentially available to the Company”. Follows the 05/21/2014 weak Q1 release and late-May/June communications from stockholders and interested parties.\n13: SRC: P-002; P-003 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R004; R008\n14: DATES: 2014-06-18 00:00:00 -> 2014-06-18 00:00:00 WD 2014-06-18 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n15: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n16: \n17: ### 3 R003 | When: 06/18/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz | What: Adviser service observed | P1 R0 | Type: None\n18: TERMS: Legal adviser to PetSmart, described as its legal advisor and shown acting at the June 18, 2014 board meeting and throughout the process (negotiations, merger agreement, voting agreement). Engagement date not disclosed; observed service treated as the mandate start.\n19: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n20: WHY: Stated: Wachtell Lipton is identified as PetSmart's legal advisor and present at the June 18, 2014 meeting. Engagement or retention date not disclosed, so an engagement row is not supported; earliest observed service is 06/18/2014. “with Wachtell, Lipton, Rosen & Katz (“Wachtell Lipton”), its legal advisor”.\n21: SRC: P-003 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R004\n22: DATES: 2014-06-18 00:00:00 -> 2014-06-18 00:00:00 WD 2014-06-18 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n23: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n24: \n25: ### 4 R004 | When: July 2014 (engagement letter effective 08/21/2014) | Who: PetSmart / J.P. Morgan Securities LLC | What: Adviser engaged | P1 R0 | Type: None\n26: TERMS: Engaged as PetSmart's financial adviser in July 2014 after the board interviewed several candidates; engagement letter effective 08/21/2014; scope covered a possible merger, acquisition of a majority of stock or assets. Delivered the fairness opinion (oral 12/13/2014; written 12/14/2014). Fee up to approximately $39 million, a substantial portion payable only on consummation.\n27: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n28: WHY: Stated: selection month July 2014, engagement letter effective 08/21/2014, opinion dates and contingent fee disclosed. Working date is the earliest bound of the July selection window (Assigned: bound). “In July, after interviewing several potential financial advisors, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as financial advisor”; “Pursuant to an engagement letter effective as of August 21, 2014, the Company retained J.P. Morgan as its financial advisor”; “For services rendered in connection with the merger and the delivery of its opinion, the Company has agreed to pay J.P. Morgan an amount up to approximately $39 million”.\n29: SRC: P-003; X-012; X-014 | PAGE: 21 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R003\n30: DATES: 2014-07-01 00:00:00 -> 2014-08-21 00:00:00 WD 2014-07-01 00:00:00 (Reported interval / Assigned: bound) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n31: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n32: \n33: ### 5 R005 | When: 07/03/2014 (through August 2014) | Who: JANA Partners LLC (activist stockholder) | What: Activist pressure | P1 R0 | Type: None\n34: TERMS: Schedule 13D disclosing a 9.9% stake and intent to discuss a review of strategic alternatives, including a sale; multiple amendments and public letters over July-August advocating a sale; met Company representatives in person on 07/10/2014 to press its views. JANA held 5,050,107 shares (5.1%) per its 01/26/2015 13D/A.\n35: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n36: WHY: Stated: JANA filed on 07/03/2014 and publicly advocated a sale; ownership per the beneficial-ownership table. “On July 3, 2014, JANA P