0 the same evening that the Buyer Group said it was working to increase within hours. Revised merger agreement and transaction agreements in substantially executable form and financing commitment documents submitted; members of the group unwilling or unable to offer more. Longview's willingness to participate with respect to $250 million of common stock was helpful in achieving $83.00. Revises R030.\n291: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n292: WHY: Stated: price and progression, documentation, and the Longview contribution's role. Formality Formal - signal 1 (substantially executable revised acquisition documents) confirmed by an actual best-and-final price; Conditions Light - committed financing documented and remaining matters were final documentation. “Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.”; “Longview’s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.”\n293: SRC: P-023; X-008; X-011 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R030; R039\n294: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 83-83 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n295: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n296: \n297: ### 38 R038 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: Bidder 2 | What: Bid | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n298: TERMS: Best and final offer: $81.50 per share, in cash; J.P. Morgan confirmed by telephone that evening that it was Bidder 2's best and final. Revised draft and financing commitment documents submitted; any Longview accommodation would not affect its price. Revises R031.\n299: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n300: WHY: Stated: price, confirmation and documentation. Formality Formal - signal 1 (revised acquisition documents) and signal 3 (actual price confirmation during finalization); Conditions Light - committed financing documented with the revision and remaining matters were final documentation. “During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.”; “Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.”\n301: SRC: P-023 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R031; R044\n302: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 81.5-81.5 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n303: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n304: \n305: ### 39 R039 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: PetSmart ad hoc committee / Buyer Group / Longview | What: Material process update | P1 R3 | Type: None\n306: TERMS: Permitted: the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group's request to work more closely with Longview and include a rollover of Longview-managed shares in its bid, after the 12/09/2014 introductory meetings J.P. Morgan arranged between Longview and each of the Buyer Group and Bidder 2. Longview and the Buyer Group then signed a confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price, which had not previously been shared with Longview; Wachtell Lipton was instructed to provide a form of voting agreement to Longview. Bidder 2 declined any price effect and would consider Longview only after signing. Resolution recorded at R043.\n307: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n308: WHY: Stated: request, approval, confidentiality agreement and voting-agreement instruction, all on 12/12/2014. One of the two permitted rows for the rollover relationship; support is not treated as a bidding-group membership change or a new NDA by a bidder for the auction screen. “the ad hoc 