R041 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent) / Argos Merger Sub Inc. | What: Merger agreement signed | P1 R3 | Type: None\n322: TERMS: Executed the Agreement and Plan of Merger dated 12/14/2014: each outstanding share converts into the right to receive $83.00 in cash at the effective time; Company termination fee $255 million for a superior-proposal termination and Parent reverse termination fee $510 million in specified financing-failure cases; closing conditioned on stockholder adoption, antitrust clearances and no prohibitory order, with an outside date of 06/14/2015. Signing is not a bid: bid-price and formality/conditionality cells are left blank (agreed consideration appears in Cash at closing).\n323: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n324: WHY: Stated: execution, consideration and payment form; fee framework and closing conditions. “On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.”\n325: SRC: P-025; X-004; X-022; X-032 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R040; R042; R043; R044\n326: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None USD | CASH: Yes 83\n327: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n328: \n329: ### 42 R042 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Parent | What: Merger announced | P1 R3 | Type: None\n330: TERMS: Press release announcing the transaction, issued concurrently with execution. No go-shop was provided; the 15 NDA signers' standstill provisions bar them from submitting or seeking permission to submit a higher bid after a definitive agreement; as of 02/02/2015 no person had made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart. Public disclosure of the signed deal is distinct from signing.\n331: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n332: WHY: Stated: announcement and the absence of post-signing proposals to the proxy date; standstills preserved as the stated mechanism. “as of February 2, 2015, the date of this proxy statement, no person has made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart”.\n333: SRC: P-025; X-009; X-010 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R041\n334: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n335: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n336: \n337: ### 43 R043 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: Longview / Parent | What: Material process update | P1 R3 | Type: None\n338: TERMS: Resolved: rollover agreement executed under which Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (about $250 million at $83.00) to Parent immediately before the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent; the Company is an express third-party beneficiary. Longview enters the “Buyer Group” definition from 12/12/2014 onward; its remaining shares receive the same $83.00 cash consideration. A rolling-over shareholder admitted to the buyer vehicle is not a bidding-group membership change.\n339: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n340: WHY: Stated: agreement, share count and treatment of other shares. The second permitted row for the rollover relationship (permitted at R039, resolved here); no new bidder NDA or bid is created. “Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (“rollover shares”) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent”; “Longview will receive the same $83.00 per share merger consideration as the other holders of the Company’s common stock for all other shares of common stock beneficially owned by it (other than the rollover shares).”\n341: SRC: X-018; X-019; X-020; X-001 | PAGE: 41 | REVIEW: Q8 | RELATED: R039; R041\n342: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n343: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n344: \n345: ### 44 R044 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: Bidder 2 | What: Not selected at signing | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n346: TERMS: The target signed with the Buyer Group; Bidder 2's $81.50 best-and-final was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group, and the board noted Bidder 2's $81.50 was its best and final. Participation had not previously ended, so this is a signing outcome, stated, not an invented earlier withdrawal; no Re-entered row follows.\n347: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n348: WHY: Stated: the choice and the price comparison; a live finalist at signing is closed as Not selected at signing with Outcome basis Stated. Decided by Target (the board selected the Buyer Group's higher-priced, more executable offer). “neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group”.\n349: SRC: P-024; X-008 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: R038; R040; R041\n350: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n351: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: Target | EXIT: Lower offer than rivals | BASIS: Stated\n352: ","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_dump.txt, lines 181-352\n181: SRC: P-013 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q1 | RELATED: R017; R019; R022; R025; R026\n182: DATES: 2014-11-03 00:00:00 -> 2014-11-03 00:00:00 WD 2014-11-03 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n183: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: Inferred final | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n184: \n185: ### 24 R024 | When: by 11/03/2014 | Who: 2 eliminated IOI submitters (unnamed cohort) | What: Dropped by target | P1 R2 | Type: Financial\n186: TERMS: Inferred: residual — 6 IOI submitters − 4 advancing at or above $80.00 = 2 eliminated submitters, being the two members of R020 whose indications did not reach the threshold (the third member advanced within the unnamed finalists). J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties; none indicated any interest or ability to remain above its initial indications. Exclusion from the final round only; no motive or identity inferred.\n187: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n188: WHY: Stated: notification of elimination after the 11/03/2014 board meeting; the number is the arithmetic residual. The two members are identified only by count within R020, so no identity is assigned. “representatives of J.P. Morgan notified the eliminated parties, none of which indicated any interest or ability to remain in the process at price levels above their respective initial indications”.\n189: SRC: P-013 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: R020; R023\n190: DATES: None -> 2014-11-03 00:00:00 WD 2014-11-03 00:00:00 (Relative only / Assigned: decision day) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n191: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: Target | EXIT: Lower offer than rivals | BASIS: Inferred: residual\n192: \n193: ### 25 R025 | When: after 11/03/2014 (day not disclosed) | Who: Bidder 3 (two of the four final-round bidders) | What: Bidding group changed | P1 R2 | Type: Financial\n194: TERMS: Formation: two final-round bidders authorized to work together as “Bidder 3” after one sought an equity partner given the size of an acquisition of PetSmart and the other had said it would drop out if not permitted to team; both had worked together successfully on prior large leveraged buyouts. Bidding units 4 → 3 (units −1; analytical convention); both members are unnamed, so the unit count falls without individual identity rows. All admitted bidders had indicated some interest in a Longview rollover, none made it a condition.\n195: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n196: WHY: Stated: authorization by the ad hoc committee after the 11/03/2014 meeting; membership not individually identified by the filing, so the row states the unit effect by number under the instruction's anonymous-cohort convention. “After deliberation and consultation with the Company’s financial and legal advisors, the ad hoc committee authorized these two bidders to work together.”; “We refer to these two bidders together as “Bidder 3.””.\n197: SRC: P-014 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q5 | RELATED: R023; R033\n198: DATES: 2014-11-03 00:00:00 -> None WD 2014-11-03 00:00:00 (Relative only / Assigned: bound) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n199: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n200: \n201: ### 26 R026 | When: November 2014 (day not disclosed) | Who: PetSmart / final-round bidders | What: Round opened | P1 R3 | Type: None\n202: TERMS: R3: Company circulated a form of merger agreement instructing bidders to submit proposed comments together with their final bids; the bid date was initially Friday 12/05/2014. Objective: obtain final bids and executable documentation from the three final-round bidding units. Round finality: Announced as final - bids were solicited as “final bids”; the 12/04-05 and 12/10-12 events are deadline revisions inside this round, not new rounds.\n203: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n204: WHY: Stated: November circulation and final-bid instruction; initial 12/05 date. The first request for final offers opens this round under the instruction's round rule, even though the invited set is unchanged. “the Company circulated a form of merger agreement to the bidders with instructions that the bidders submit any proposed comments on the merger agreement together with their final bids”; “had initially set Friday, December 5 as the date for submission of bids”.\n205: SRC: P-015; P-016 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q1; Q7 | RELATED: R023; R025; R028\n206: DATES: 2014-11-01 00:00:00 -> 2014-11-30 00:00:00 WD 2014-11-15 00:00:00 (Approximate window / Assigned: midpoint) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n207: DUE: 2014-12-05 00:00:00 | TREAT: None | FINALITY: Announced as final | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n208: \n209: ### 27 R027 | When: November 2014 (following the Q3 earnings release) | Who: All final-round bidders / J.P. Morgan | What: Information access changed | P1 R3 | Type: None\n210: TERMS: Projections revised after bidding began: after the third-quarter earnings release, at bidders' request and the board's direction, J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the fiscal-year-2014 projections to reflect actual performance and better visibility on the Profit Improvement Plan (FY2014E revenue $7,081M vs $7,088M before; EBITDA $967M vs $958M; net income $445M vs $432M; cash flow from operations unchanged at $617M). The FY2020-24 extrapolations and J.P. Morgan's downside sensitivities were not provided to bidders - see Summary comparability.\n211: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n212: WHY: Stated: revision and recipients; the update note gives before/after figures. A projection revision after bidding began is recorded as an information-access change; the same update went to all final-round bidders, so it is not a differentiated-access row. “Following the Company’s third quarter earnings announcement and, at the request of bidders and the direction of the board and the Company, representatives of J.P. Morgan provided the bidders with updates to the Company’s fiscal year 2014 financial projections.”\n213: SRC: P-015; X-015; X-016 | PAGE: 37 | REVIEW: Q7 | RELATED: R026\n214: DATES: 2014-11-01 00:00:00 -> 2014-11-30 00:00:00 WD 2014-11-15 00:00:00 (Approximate window / Assigned: midpoint) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n215: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n216: \n217: ### 28 R028 | When: 12/04/2014-12/05/2014 | Who: PetSmart ad hoc committee | What: Deadline revised | P1 R3 | Type: None\n218: TERMS: Ad hoc committee, after consulting the Company's financial and legal advisers, replaced the initial 12/05/2014 bid date with the evening of 12/10/2014 (five days rather than ten before the anticipated 12/15/2014 completion), so the process could finish sooner and reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure; bidders were simultaneously asked to submit mark-ups of the draft merger agreement and other transaction documents and financing commitments, if possible, in advance. Old due date 12/05/2014 (superseded before arrival; no milestone row); new due date 12/10/2014. Deadline treatment records what followed 12/10/2014 (extended at R035).\n219: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n220: WHY: Stated: the two-day committee decision, the reason and both dates. Working date is the last day of the decision span (Assigned: decision day). Background premise: the 12/03/2014 board meeting had reviewed positive operating and Profit Improvement Plan indications and made no decisions because it had no bids in hand. “the ad hoc committee concluded that these matters could be accomplished in a shorter period of time, which would reduce the risk of leaks or unintended public disclosure.”; “Accordingly, the Company set the evening of Wednesday, December 10”.\n221: SRC: P-016 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: R026; R029\n222: DATES: 2014-12-04 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-05 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-05 00:00:00 (Reported interval / Assigned: decision day) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n223: DUE: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 | TREAT: Extended | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n224: \n225: ### 29 R029 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: PetSmart / final-round bidders | What: Deadline | P1 R3 | Type: None\n226: TERMS: Final-bid deadline reached: Buyer Group and Bidder 2 submitted final bid letters with revised merger agreement and transaction documents, and Bidder 3 gave a verbal indication (R030-R033). The same evening the ad hoc committee instructed improved bids by 12/12/2014 (R035) - this due date was extended, with no late-bid acceptance issue.\n227: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n228: WHY: Stated: bids received on the date; extension decided that evening. Deadline treatment Extended because a Deadline revised row (R035) moved this date. “On December 10, PetSmart received final bid letters along with revised versions of the merger agreement and other transaction documents from the Buyer Group and from Bidder 2 and a verbal indication from Bidder 3.”\n229: SRC: P-020; P-021 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: R028; R035\n230: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n231: DUE: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 | TREAT: Extended | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n232: \n233: ### 30 R030 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: Buyer Group (BC Partners-led consortium) | What: Bid | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n234: TERMS: Final bid: $80.70 per share, in cash; final bid letter and revised merger agreement and other transaction documents, which were more favorable to the Company (less conditional, more likely to be completed, more certainty of protection) and reflected substantially more acceptance of the Company's positions than Bidder 2's. Financing commitment documents had been provided 12/06/2014. Bid not dependent on a Longview rollover, though partnering was not ruled out. Revised at R037.\n235: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n236: WHY: Stated: price and cash form; documentation and financing facts. Formality Formal - signal 1 (bidder-returned acquisition agreement and transaction documents, substantially executable) plus the requested final-bid response. Conditions Light - no Heavy trigger; committed financing documented; remaining matters were final documentation (board approval on 12/13 was subject to resolving open points). “The Buyer Group offered $80.70 per share, in cash, and Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash.”; “The form of merger agreement and other transaction documentation submitted by the Buyer Group were more favorable to the Company”.\n237: SRC: P-017; P-020 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R017; R028; R037\n238: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 80.7-80.7 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n239: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n240: \n241: ### 31 R031 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: Bidder 2 | What: Bid | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n242: TERMS: Final bid: $80.35 per share, in cash; final bid letter and revised merger agreement and transaction documents. Bid not dependent on a Longview rollover; Bidder 2 said any partnering with Longview would occur only after signing a merger agreement. Financing commitment documents were provided with its 12/12 revision (R038). Revised at R038.\n243: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: not stated; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n244: WHY: Stated: price and cash form; documentation; rollover position. Formality Formal - revised acquisition agreement and transaction documents submitted with the final-bid response. Conditions Light - no Heavy trigger; treat as subject to final documentation; financing not stated at this date (silence neither raises nor lowers; documents followed on 12/12). “Bidder 2 offered $80.35 per share, in cash”; “Each bidder indicated that its bid was not dependent on a rollover by Longview”.\n245: SRC: P-020 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R022; R029; R038\n246: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 80.35-80.35 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n247: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n248: \n249: ### 32 R032 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: Bidder 3 | What: Valuation statement | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n250: TERMS: Verbal indication in response to the final-bid solicitation: Bidder 3's valuation would not be above the then-current stock price of approximately $78.00 per share. A communicated valuation ceiling, not a bid for the bid-price cells; the non-submission is recorded at R033.\n251: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n252: WHY: Stated: the valuation statement and the comparison, on the final-bid date. Treated as a valuation statement (no offer made; the filing's price reference is the market price) so per-share cells are left blank and the value stays in text. “Bidder 3 verbally communicated to J.P. Morgan that their valuation would not be above the current stock price of approximately $78 per share.”\n253: SRC: P-020 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R025; R033\n254: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n255: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n256: \n257: ### 33 R033 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: Bidder 3 | What: Did not submit | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n258: TERMS: No written final offer: after J.P. Morgan told Bidder 3 its indication was unlikely to be competitive, it submitted no written offer. Its communicated valuation was at or below the ~$78.00 market price and below the $80.70/$80.35 rival bids. The combined unit is closed here; a written submission did not occur in this solicitation.\n259: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n260: WHY: Stated: non-submission and the discouraging communication. Decided by Both - target discouragement followed by non-participation (mixed mechanism). Exit reason Value at or below market price (benchmark: current stock price ~$78; also below rivals, preserved in text). “J.P. Morgan communicated to Bidder 3 that it was unlikely to be competitive and accordingly Bidder 3 did not submit a written offer.”\n261: SRC: P-020 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q4; Q5 | RELATED: R032; R025\n262: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n263: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: Both | EXIT: Value at or below market price | BASIS: Stated\n264: \n265: ### 34 R034 | When: by 12/10/2014 | Who: Unnamed financial bidder 1 (suggested $80.00-$85.00) | What: Did not submit | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n266: TERMS: Inferred: identity — last individually observed advancing to the final round on 11/03/2014 (R018); not mentioned again. It may be one of the two unnamed finalists that combined as Bidder 3 (R025) and be closed by R033; alternatively its exit is already inside the anonymous final-round units. Count 0: no count moves from a cohort to a name on this basis. See Q5.\n267: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n268: WHY: Convention (Count-0 identity row): the filing never mentions this submitter again after the advancement, and the two anonymous finalists absorbed two of the four advancing units. Recommended reading: within the Bidder 3 unit closed at R033. “another bidder, which suggested a range of $80.00 to $85.00 per share”; “the four bidders that had indicated a price or range at or above $80.00 per share to proceed to the final round”.\n269: SRC: P-012; P-013; P-014 | PAGE: 24 | REVIEW: Q4; Q5 | RELATED: R018; R025; R033\n270: DATES: None -> 2014-12-10 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Relative only / Assigned: decision day) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n271: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: Both | EXIT: Value at or below market price | BASIS: Inferred: identity\n272: \n273: ### 35 R035 | When: 12/10/2014 | Who: PetSmart ad hoc committee / J.P. Morgan | What: Deadline revised | P1 R3 | Type: None\n274: TERMS: After receiving the 12/10 bids, the ad hoc committee found there could be no assurance the board would approve either bid unless improved, citing the closeness of the bids, positive developments from the 12/03/2014 board meeting and the shared view that neither bid was the bidder's best; J.P. Morgan was instructed to require increased bids due 12/12/2014. On the evening of 12/11/2014 J.P. Morgan also confirmed Longview's continued interest in rolling over shares, subject to approval. Old due date 12/10/2014 (extended at R029); new due date 12/12/2014. Deadline treatment records what followed 12/12/2014 (enforced at R036).\n275: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n276: WHY: Stated: instruction and new date; reason (closeness of bids and recent positive developments, including the Profit Improvement Plan's expected at least $200 million annual incremental profit) and the 12/11 Longview call. Working date is the reported decision day. “the ad hoc committee instructed J.P. Morgan to inform each bidder that it would need to increase its bid, and to instruct the bidders to submit improved bids on December 12, 2014.”; “indications that the Profit Improvement Plan would likely be successful in achieving at least $200 million in annual incremental profit”.\n277: SRC: P-016; P-021 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: R029; R036\n278: DATES: 2014-12-10 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-11 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-10 00:00:00 (Reported interval / Assigned: decision day) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n279: DUE: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 | TREAT: Enforced | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n280: \n281: ### 36 R036 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: PetSmart / final-round bidders | What: Deadline | P1 R3 | Type: None\n282: TERMS: Improved-bid deadline reached: Buyer Group and Bidder 2 submitted best-and-final offers with revised drafts and financing commitment documents (R037, R038). The board met on 12/13/2014 and acted on the bids in hand - enforced, with no further extension.\n283: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n284: WHY: Stated: submissions on 12/12/2014 and the board meeting the next day. Deadline treatment Enforced. “each bidder submitted a revised draft of the merger agreement and other transaction agreements, and copies of their respective financing commitment documents”.\n285: SRC: P-023; P-024 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q2 | RELATED: R035; R037; R038\n286: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n287: DUE: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 | TREAT: Enforced | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n288: \n289: ### 37 R037 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: Buyer Group (BC Partners-led consortium) | What: Bid | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n290: TERMS: Support: Longview (rollover) — best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash, after an initial oral $82.50 the same evening that the Buyer Group said it was working to increase within hours. Revised merger agreement and transaction agreements in substantially executable form and financing commitment documents submitted; members of the group unwilling or unable to offer more. Longview's willingness to participate with respect to $250 million of common stock was helpful in achieving $83.00. Revises R030.\n291: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n292: WHY: Stated: price and progression, documentation, and the Longview contribution's role. Formality Formal - signal 1 (substantially executable revised acquisition documents) confirmed by an actual best-and-final price; Conditions Light - committed financing documented and remaining matters were final documentation. “Later in the evening, the Buyer Group submitted a best and final offer of $83.00 per share, in cash.”; “Longview’s willingness to participate in the Buyer Group with respect to $250 million of the common stock was helpful in achieving an $83.00 per share price.”\n293: SRC: P-023; X-008; X-011 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R030; R039\n294: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 83-83 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n295: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n296: \n297: ### 38 R038 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: Bidder 2 | What: Bid | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n298: TERMS: Best and final offer: $81.50 per share, in cash; J.P. Morgan confirmed by telephone that evening that it was Bidder 2's best and final. Revised draft and financing commitment documents submitted; any Longview accommodation would not affect its price. Revises R031.\n299: FORMALITY: Formal | CONDITIONS: Light | DETAIL: Fin: committed; DD required: not stated; DD open: no; Excl: not stated\n300: WHY: Stated: price, confirmation and documentation. Formality Formal - signal 1 (revised acquisition documents) and signal 3 (actual price confirmation during finalization); Conditions Light - committed financing documented with the revision and remaining matters were final documentation. “During the evening of December 12, 2014, Bidder 2 submitted an offer of $81.50 per share, in cash.”; “Representatives of J.P. Morgan confirmed via a conversation with Bidder 2 on the evening of December 12, 2014 that $81.50 per share was its best and final offer.”\n301: SRC: P-023 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q6 | RELATED: R031; R044\n302: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: 81.5-81.5 Point Stated USD | CASH: Yes None\n303: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n304: \n305: ### 39 R039 | When: 12/12/2014 | Who: PetSmart ad hoc committee / Buyer Group / Longview | What: Material process update | P1 R3 | Type: None\n306: TERMS: Permitted: the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group's request to work more closely with Longview and include a rollover of Longview-managed shares in its bid, after the 12/09/2014 introductory meetings J.P. Morgan arranged between Longview and each of the Buyer Group and Bidder 2. Longview and the Buyer Group then signed a confidentiality agreement permitting exchange of detailed information including bid price, which had not previously been shared with Longview; Wachtell Lipton was instructed to provide a form of voting agreement to Longview. Bidder 2 declined any price effect and would consider Longview only after signing. Resolution recorded at R043.\n307: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n308: WHY: Stated: request, approval, confidentiality agreement and voting-agreement instruction, all on 12/12/2014. One of the two permitted rows for the rollover relationship; support is not treated as a bidding-group membership change or a new NDA by a bidder for the auction screen. “the ad hoc committee approved the Buyer Group’s request, and, later that day, Longview and the Buyer Group entered into a confidentiality agreement permitting the exchange of detailed information between them, including bid price”.\n309: SRC: P-019; P-022 | PAGE: 25 | REVIEW: Q8 | RELATED: R037; R043\n310: DATES: 2014-12-12 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-12 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-12 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n311: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n312: \n313: ### 40 R040 | When: 12/13/2014 | Who: PetSmart board | What: Target decision | P1 R3 | Type: None\n314: TERMS: Board unanimously determined the merger agreement and the merger advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders and resolved to recommend adoption; the determination was subject to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved. J.P. Morgan delivered its oral fairness opinion on the $83.00 consideration (written opinion the next day); the board would reconvene if needed.\n315: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n316: WHY: Stated: approval, qualification and opinion timing. Selection of the Buyer Group is reflected here and in the signing row; separate from the round opening. “the board unanimously determined that the merger agreement and the transactions contemplated thereby, including the merger, were advisable and in the best interests of PetSmart and its stockholders”; “subject, however, to confirmation that the remaining open points in the merger agreement had been satisfactorily resolved”.\n317: SRC: P-024; X-013 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R041; R042\n318: DATES: 2014-12-13 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-13 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-13 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n319: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n320: \n321: ### 41 R041 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Argos Holdings Inc. (Parent) / Argos Merger Sub Inc. | What: Merger agreement signed | P1 R3 | Type: None\n322: TERMS: Executed the Agreement and Plan of Merger dated 12/14/2014: each outstanding share converts into the right to receive $83.00 in cash at the effective time; Company termination fee $255 million for a superior-proposal termination and Parent reverse termination fee $510 million in specified financing-failure cases; closing conditioned on stockholder adoption, antitrust clearances and no prohibitory order, with an outside date of 06/14/2015. Signing is not a bid: bid-price and formality/conditionality cells are left blank (agreed consideration appears in Cash at closing).\n323: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n324: WHY: Stated: execution, consideration and payment form; fee framework and closing conditions. “On December 14, 2014, the parties executed the merger agreement, the voting agreement and related transaction agreements and issued a press release announcing the transaction.”\n325: SRC: P-025; X-004; X-022; X-032 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R040; R042; R043; R044\n326: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None USD | CASH: Yes 83\n327: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n328: \n329: ### 42 R042 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: PetSmart / Parent | What: Merger announced | P1 R3 | Type: None\n330: TERMS: Press release announcing the transaction, issued concurrently with execution. No go-shop was provided; the 15 NDA signers' standstill provisions bar them from submitting or seeking permission to submit a higher bid after a definitive agreement; as of 02/02/2015 no person had made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart. Public disclosure of the signed deal is distinct from signing.\n331: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n332: WHY: Stated: announcement and the absence of post-signing proposals to the proxy date; standstills preserved as the stated mechanism. “as of February 2, 2015, the date of this proxy statement, no person has made an unsolicited offer or proposal to acquire PetSmart”.\n333: SRC: P-025; X-009; X-010 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: None | RELATED: R041\n334: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n335: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n336: \n337: ### 43 R043 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: Longview / Parent | What: Material process update | P1 R3 | Type: None\n338: TERMS: Resolved: rollover agreement executed under which Longview contributes 3,012,050 shares (about $250 million at $83.00) to Parent immediately before the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent; the Company is an express third-party beneficiary. Longview enters the “Buyer Group” definition from 12/12/2014 onward; its remaining shares receive the same $83.00 cash consideration. A rolling-over shareholder admitted to the buyer vehicle is not a bidding-group membership change.\n339: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n340: WHY: Stated: agreement, share count and treatment of other shares. The second permitted row for the rollover relationship (permitted at R039, resolved here); no new bidder NDA or bid is created. “Longview has agreed to contribute 3,012,050 shares (“rollover shares”) to Parent immediately prior to the effective time in exchange for equity interests in Parent”; “Longview will receive the same $83.00 per share merger consideration as the other holders of the Company’s common stock for all other shares of common stock beneficially owned by it (other than the rollover shares).”\n341: SRC: X-018; X-019; X-020; X-001 | PAGE: 41 | REVIEW: Q8 | RELATED: R039; R041\n342: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n343: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: None | EXIT: None | BASIS: None\n344: \n345: ### 44 R044 | When: 12/14/2014 | Who: Bidder 2 | What: Not selected at signing | P1 R3 | Type: Financial\n346: TERMS: The target signed with the Buyer Group; Bidder 2's $81.50 best-and-final was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group, and the board noted Bidder 2's $81.50 was its best and final. Participation had not previously ended, so this is a signing outcome, stated, not an invented earlier withdrawal; no Re-entered row follows.\n347: FORMALITY: None | CONDITIONS: None | DETAIL: None\n348: WHY: Stated: the choice and the price comparison; a live finalist at signing is closed as Not selected at signing with Outcome basis Stated. Decided by Target (the board selected the Buyer Group's higher-priced, more executable offer). “neither of which was willing to make a definitive offer at a price above $81.50, which was lower than the $83.00 price offered by the Buyer Group”.\n349: SRC: P-024; X-008 | PAGE: 26 | REVIEW: Q4 | RELATED: R038; R040; R041\n350: DATES: 2014-12-14 00:00:00 -> 2014-12-14 00:00:00 WD 2014-12-14 00:00:00 (Reported day / Reported) | PRICE: None-None None None None | CASH: None None\n351: DUE: None | TREAT: None | FINALITY: None | DECIDED: Target | EXIT: Lower offer than rivals | BASIS: Stated\n352: "}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"limit\": 180, \"offset\": 181, \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/ledger_dump.txt\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825131735,"end":1789825131911}}}}
