{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825155179,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e47f48001QrPZ90qAVysLhR","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9e42594001QUv7J1rlzDiqWv","type":"tool","id":"call_00_2IV6fLN7s6Zu474REUOA2803","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && grep -n \"R011\\|R012\\|R024\\|Lower offer than rivals\" build_ledger.py build_xlsx.py | head -40"},"output":"build_ledger.py:193:    related='R001; R007; R012', review='', count=None,\nbuild_ledger.py:217:    terms=(\"R1 anchor: confidentiality-agreement wave (R014) \\u2014 first target-organized step admitting participants (no dated first outreach wave is reported; contacts came to J.P. Morgan). Rejected candidate anchors: R008 (08/13 decision; planned outreach was for late September/early October, not within a week), R009 (08/19 announcement replacing outreach), R012 (10/03 board update). Objective: signed NDAs/standstills, due diligence and management presentations, then non-binding indications of interest due 10/30/2014. Round finality: Not final - preliminary non-binding stage, no final/binding announcement.\"),\nbuild_ledger.py:221:    related='R008; R009; R012; R014', review='Q1', count=None, finality='Not final',\nbuild_ledger.py:251:    related='R011; R014; R023', review='Q2', count=None, due=D(2014,10,30), treatment='Enforced',\nbuild_ledger.py:296:    related='R017; R018; R019; R024', review='Q3; Q4', count=3,\nbuild_ledger.py:341:    decided='Target', exit_reason='Lower offer than rivals', outcome_basis='Inferred: residual',\nbuild_ledger.py:550:    decided='Target', exit_reason='Lower offer than rivals', outcome_basis='Stated',\nbuild_xlsx.py:159:       'Would not improve earlier offer','Lower offer than rivals','Terms or process','Other stated reason','Not stated'],\nbuild_xlsx.py:193:s('Initiation assessment', \"Mixed - target-led exploration by the board and the ad hoc committee, following activist pressure (JANA, Longview) and inbound interest (Industry Participant's 08/07/2014 approach and 27 contacts), with the 08/19/2014 public announcement deliberately used to widen the field. Sequence: R001-R012 (round 0), then R013 (round 1 opening).\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:206:s('Round 1 (Round opened row R013) - Not final', \"Anchor: the confidentiality-agreement wave (R014); rejected candidate anchors kept as rows: R008 (08/13 decision), R009 (08/19 announcement), R012 (10/03 board update). Scope: 15 financial NDA signers; October diligence, management presentations and Profit Improvement Plan access; non-binding IOIs due 10/30/2014 (R015, R016). Round-bidder tally: 6 submitting units (R017-R020; Bidder 2's revision R022 carries Count 0).\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:207:s('Round 2 (Round opened row R023) - Inferred final', \"Opened 11/03/2014: four bidders at or above $80.00 advance (Buyer Group R017, Bidder 2 R019/R022, and two unnamed finalists tracked in R020); two submitters eliminated (R024); final-round diligence and merger-agreement circulation; two finalists combine as Bidder 3, units 4 to 3 (R025).\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:209:s('Deadline history and treatment', \"10/30/2014 IOIs (R016) - Enforced: six submissions, J.P. Morgan feedback calls 10/30-11/02, board advanced four on 11/03. 12/05/2014 final bids (on R026) - Extended: superseded 12/04-05 before arrival and moved by R028; no milestone row. 12/10/2014 final bids (R029) - Extended: bids received; committee moved the deadline to 12/12 by R035. 12/12/2014 improved bids (R036) - Enforced: best-and-final offers received; board acted 12/13. No 'Late bids accepted' case; round 2 has no submission deadline; 'No deadline stated' does not apply. Earlier R1 anchors rejected: R008, R009, R012.\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:210:s('Endings and tallies', \"Winner: Buyer Group (no exit row). Stated outcomes: Bidder 3 Did not submit (R033; 1 unit), Bidder 2 Not selected at signing (R044; 1 unit). Inferred outcomes: 9 Did not submit (R021; residual), 2 Dropped by target (R024; residual); one Count-0 identity row (R034). Round-bidder tallies are scoped to each stage, not unique firms across the deal.\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:218:s('Other first-round cohort', \"The third bidder initially at or above $80.00 is not individually distinguishable (tracked within R020, R023, R025); two submitters below the threshold were eliminated (R024, inferred residual); nine NDA signers did not submit IOIs (R021, inferred residual). These are scoped cohorts, not unique firms; one member of R020 advanced within the unnamed finalists.\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:221:s('Industry Participant', \"Unnamed privately held industry participant. PetSmart's own approach in Spring 2014 (R001); inbound approach 08/07/2014 (R007); excluded from the process on 08/22-27/2014, reaffirmed 10/03/2014 (R010, R012). Never entered - no NDA or bid; no outcome row.\", '')\nbuild_xlsx.py:236:   \"2 eliminated submitters at the 11/03 advancement (R024, inferred residual).\"))\nbuild_xlsx.py:291: \"Recommended: one process (2014 sale process); R1 anchored on the first-week-of-October confidentiality wave (R014), not the 08/13 decision, 08/19 announcement or 10/03 board update (all retained as rows R008/R009/R012 so the boundary can move). R2 opens with the 11/03 advancement (Inferred final); R3 opens with the November request for 'final bids' (Announced as final); the 12/04-05 and 12/10-12 events are deadline revisions inside R3, not new rounds. Keep R1 'Not final' (preliminary IOI stage).\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:305: \"R011, R014, R017-R020, R022, R023, R024; Summary counts block\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:306: \"If some signers were not eligible for the IOI solicitation, the 9-non-submitter residual shrinks; if '5 groups' were preferred, the round-1 tally falls by one (the six otherwise reconcile to 4 advancing + 2 eliminated). Any change to the R020/R024 split changes the inferred-elimination count.\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:309: \"Recommended: (a) 10/30/2014 - 9 unnamed NDA signers Did not submit, Inferred: residual (15 NDA signers - 6 submitters), Count 9, Decided by Unknown, reason Not stated (R021); (b) 11/03/2014 - 2 unnamed submitters Dropped by target, Inferred: residual (6 submitters - 4 advancing), Count 2, Decided by Target, reason Lower offer than rivals (R024); (c) by 12/10/2014 - Unnamed financial bidder 1, Count-0 identity row (recommended reading: closed inside Bidder 3; R034). Stated comparators: Bidder 3 Did not submit (R033) and Bidder 2 Not selected at signing (R044). No identities, motives or permanent withdrawals are inferred.\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:311: \"R021, R024, R034 (plus stated R033, R044); Summary balance\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:317: \"R018, R020, R023, R024, R025, R033, R034; Summary participants\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:318: \"If a reviewer accepts a different mapping, R034's recommended reading changes but no count or balance changes (Count 0); if a combiner was not a finalist, the R2/R3 unit counts and R024's residual basis would need restating.\",\nbuild_xlsx.py:329: \"R011, R013, R014, R021, R022, R025, R026, R027, R034; Date fields\",\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"build_ledger.py:193:    related='R001; R007; R012', review='', count=None,\nbuild_ledger.py:217:    terms=(\"R1 anchor: confidentiality-agreement wave (R014) \\u2014 first target-organized step admitting participants (no dated first outreach wave is reported; contacts came to J.P. Morgan). Rejected candidate anchors: R008 (08/13 decision; planned outreach was for late September/early October, not within a week), R009 (08/19 announcement replacing outreach), R012 (10/03 board update). Objective: signed NDAs/standstills, due diligence and management presentations, then non-binding indications of interest due 10/30/2014. Round finality: Not final - preliminary non-binding stage, no final/binding announcement.\"),\nbuild_ledger.py:221:    relat