{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825199468,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e529b5001kbhAdDQHIG9IeC","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9e5097b001VWXhqbVMVcT19X","type":"tool","id":"call_00_wFANYq3djTZ81pHIPbOv5757","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":" \"R011, R012, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\",","oldString":" \"R011, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\",","path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py"},"output":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n+++ /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n@@ -301,9 +301,9 @@\n  'Pending',''),\n ('Q3','Count and population bases (conflicts and residuals)',\n  \"Recommended readings: (a) six IOI submitters (background, p.24) over '5 bidder groups' (Reasons, p.27) - the background is specific and contemporaneous, and the six include the two below-$80 submitters; (b) all 15 NDA signers were eligible for the 10/30 solicitation (they had been told the due date), so the residual is 9 non-submitters (R022); (c) the two eliminees are the two residual submitters within R021 whose indications were below $80.00 - a count-based residual, not named identities; (d) 27 contacts (p.23) with the 'more than 25' wording (p.27) treated as a consistent lower bound; (e) Bidder 2, Bidder 3 and Unnamed financial bidder 1 are typed Financial by inference from the all-financial 15-signer cohort - the filing never states their type individually.\",\n  \"Counts at P-008, P-010, P-012, P-013, P-014; conflict passages P-012 vs X-008; type basis P-010 ('15 potentially interested financial buyers'). The instruction requires residual cohorts to be disjoint from individually recorded members and counts to be scoped, with bases surfaced where uncertain.\",\n- \"R011, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\",\n+ \"R011, R012, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\",\n  \"If some signers were not eligible for the IOI solicitation, the 9-non-submitter residual shrinks; if '5 groups' were preferred, the round-1 tally falls by one (the six otherwise reconcile to 4 advancing + 2 eliminated). Any change to the R021/R025 split changes the inferred-elimination count.\",\n  'Pending',''),\n ('Q4','Every inferred closing row (grouped by transition)',\n  \"Recommended: (a) 10/30/2014 - 9 unnamed NDA signers Did not submit, Inferred: residual (15 NDA signers - 6 submitters), Count 9, Decided by Unknown, reason Not stated (R022); (b) 11/03/2014 - 2 unnamed submitters Dropped by target, Inferred: residual (6 submitters - 4 advancing), Count 2, Decided by Target, reason Lower offer than rivals (R025); (c) by 12/10/2014 - Unnamed financial bidder 1, Count-0 identity row (recommended reading: closed inside Bidder 3; R035). Stated comparators: Bidder 3 Did not submit (R034) and Bidder 2 Not selected at signing (R045). No identities, motives or permanent withdrawals are inferred.\",\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \" \\\"R011, R012, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\\\",\", \"oldString\": \" \\\"R011, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\\\",\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825198517,"end":1789825199468}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825199479,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e52ad10010ie56ovLXHYUb5","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9e5097b001VWXhqbVMVcT19X","type":"tool","id":"call_01_MNTma118vwAHb0ZrADb83526","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":" \"R011, R012, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\",","oldString":" \"R011, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\",","path":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py"},"output":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py","patch":"Index: /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n===================================================================\n--- /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n+++ /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\n@@ -325,9 +325,9 @@\n  'Pending',''),\n ('Q7','Working dates and display order conventions',\n  \"Recommended: NDA wave Working date 10/04/2014 (midpoint of 10/01-10/07) with the interval preserved; 27-contact Working date 09/22/2014 (midpoint of mid-August-end October); R3 and the projection-update rows 11/15/2014 (November midpoints); Bidder 3 formation 11/03/2014 (Assigned: bound - after the 11/03 meeting, day not disclosed); inferred closings use the deadline/decision day (10/30, 11/03, 12/10). Same-day blocks (10/30 deadline vs submissions; 12/10 bids, valuation, non-submission and revision; 12/14 signing, announcement, rollover resolution and Bidder 2's outcome) use a deterministic display order; the relative order within them is not established by the filing and the shared dates are a display convention. A reviewer may adopt the alternative first-day reading for the NDA wave (10/01) and the 10/30/2014 bound for the contact row.\",\n  \"Instruction's date rules; intervals and relative expressions in P-008, P-010, P-014, P-015, P-021, P-022, P-023, P-025. Bounds are tightened where a later passage shows the event (e.g., the 11/03 board had the IOI set before it, so all submissions sit at 10/30).\",\n- \"R011, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\",\n+ \"R011, R012, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\",\n  \"Moving the NDA wave to 10/01 would place it before the 10/03 board update and might suggest NDAs preceded that update; moving R3's Working date later narrows the gap to the 12/04-05 revision but changes no facts. Any reassignment must keep Working dates non-decreasing and inside each row's own bounds.\",\n  'Pending',''),\n ('Q8','Comparability, consideration and other-scope coverage',\n  \"Recommended: no other-scope bids (nothing to exclude from core counts); single currency USD; the only non-cash element is Longview's rollover of 3,012,050 shares into Parent equity, treated as support rather than a bidding-group membership change or a partial-company offer; equity value is a labelled calculation (99,455,151 x $83.00 = about $8.25 billion), not a filing-stated total; market references ($77.67 close on 12/12/2014; 38.8% premium to 07/02/2014; about $78.00 reference on 12/10) are benchmarks, not offers; funding inputs (debt up to $6.95 billion, equity up to about $1.83 billion, rollover $250 million, ~$425 million cash) are as disclosed.\",\n","status":"modified","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited /tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\": \" \\\"R011, R012, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\\\",\", \"oldString\": \" \\\"R011, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\\\",\", \"path\": \"/tmp/opencode/petsmart/build_xlsx.py\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825198801,"end":1789825199479}}}}
