{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1789825253911,"sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","part":{"partID":"prt_0b9e5ffef001lVPE6qWNs3KKyz","sessionID":"ses_f462a6b74ffedf3OBDp51fgDmj","messageID":"msg_0b9e5f05b0017E9Cm4HUQdihS5","type":"tool","id":"call_00_PlO3HrlKXyZzVI0h640W7919","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\nwq = wb['Questions']\nfor r in range(2, wq.max_row+1):\n    print('='*100)\n    for c in range(1, 7):\n        v = wq.cell(row=r, column=c).value\n        if v: print(f\"[{wq.cell(row=1,column=c).value}] {v}\")\nEOF"},"output":"====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q1\n[Review topic] Process and round map; R1 anchor and finality values\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: one process (2014 sale process); R1 anchored on the first-week-of-October confidentiality wave (R015), not the 08/13 decision, 08/19 announcement or 10/03 board update (all retained as rows R008/R009/R013 so the boundary can move). R2 opens with the 11/03 advancement (Inferred final); R3 opens with the November request for 'final bids' (Announced as final); the 12/04-05 and 12/10-12 events are deadline revisions inside R3, not new rounds. Keep R1 'Not final' (preliminary IOI stage).\n[Why and source] The instruction prefers the first target-organized admission step when no dated first outreach wave exists; the filing reports contacts coming to J.P. Morgan ('J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants', P-008) and dates the CA wave (P-010). The first final-offer request opens a round even with the same bidders (P-015; initial 12/05 date in P-016); the later improvement request is a deadline revision, not a round (P-021). Alternatives: anchor R1 at the 08/13 decision or 08/19 announcement; open R3 at the 12/10 deadline instead of the November request; merge R2 into R3.\n[Affected rows/fields] R014, R015, R016, R024, R026, R027, R029, R036; Summary process/round map\n[Consequence of changing it] Moving the R1 anchor changes the round-1 scope (e.g., an 08/13 anchor would pull pre-NDA contacts into R1). A separate final-solicitation round raised at 12/10 instead of November would shift the deadline history between rounds; merging R2/R3 would drop the advancement/Documentation transition, and the round-bidder tallies (6 IOI units; 4 advancing; 2 written finals) would need restating.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q2\n[Review topic] Deadline history and treatments\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: 10/30/2014 IOI date - Enforced (R017; board advanced on 11/03 without revision). 12/05/2014 final-bid date - Extended; superseded on 12/04-05 before arrival, so it gets no milestone row and is recorded on the Deadline revised row R029. 12/10/2014 - Extended (R030; moved to 12/12 by R036). 12/12/2014 - Enforced (R037; best-and-final bids received and the board acted on 12/13). No deadline was 'Late bids accepted': Bidder 3's verbal valuation was received on the 12/10 date itself, and it then submitted nothing rather than a late bid.\n[Why and source] Dates and sequence in P-011, P-012, P-013, P-016, P-020, P-021, P-023, P-024. The instruction treats a post-deadline request for improved bids by a new date as a Deadline revised (extension), and a date superseded before arrival needs no milestone row. The 12/05 date was set but never reached; its replacement was decided 12/04-05.\n[Affected rows/fields] R017, R022, R029, R030, R036, R037; Summary deadline map\n[Consequence of changing it] If the 12/05 date were treated as reached (not superseded), it would need its own Deadline row/Enforced value; if the 12/10 improvement request were treated as a fresh Deadline set or new round, the R3 boundary and tallies change.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q3\n[Review topic] Count and population bases (conflicts and residuals)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended readings: (a) six IOI submitters (background, p.24) over '5 bidder groups' (Reasons, p.27) - the background is specific and contemporaneous, and the six include the two below-$80 submitters; (b) all 15 NDA signers were eligible for the 10/30 solicitation (they had been told the due date), so the residual is 9 non-submitters (R022); (c) the two eliminees are the two residual submitters within R021 whose indications were below $80.00 - a count-based residual, not named identities; (d) 27 contacts (p.23) with the 'more than 25' wording (p.27) treated as a consistent lower bound; (e) Bidder 2, Bidder 3 and Unnamed financial bidder 1 are typed Financial by inference from the all-financial 15-signer cohort - the filing never states their type individually.\n[Why and source] Counts at P-008, P-010, P-012, P-013, P-014; conflict passages P-012 vs X-008; type basis P-010 ('15 potentially interested financial buyers'). The instruction requires residual cohorts to be disjoint from individually recorded members and counts to be scoped, with bases surfaced where uncertain.\n[Affected rows/fields] R011, R012, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\n[Consequence of changing it] If some signers were not eligible for the IOI solicitation, the 9-non-submitter residual shrinks; if '5 groups' were preferred, the round-1 tally falls by one (the six otherwise reconcile to 4 advancing + 2 eliminated). Any change to the R021/R025 split changes the inferred-elimination count.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q4\n[Review topic] Every inferred closing row (grouped by transition)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: (a) 10/30/2014 - 9 unnamed NDA signers Did not submit, Inferred: residual (15 NDA signers - 6 submitters), Count 9, Decided by Unknown, reason Not stated (R022); (b) 11/03/2014 - 2 unnamed submitters Dropped by target, Inferred: residual (6 submitters - 4 advancing), Count 2, Decided by Target, Exit reason Not stated (the lower-price context is preserved in Terms; R025); (c) by 12/10/2014 - Unnamed financial bidder 1, Count-0 identity row (recommended reading: closed inside Bidder 3; R035). Stated comparators: Bidder 3 Did not submit (R034) and Bidder 2 Not selected at signing (R045). No identities, motives or permanent withdrawals are inferred.\n[Why and source] Instruction's closing rules: residual non-submissions by subtraction; eliminations by residual at the advancement; a named-but-silent party gets a Count-0 identity row naming the covering cohort; stated outcomes take no opener. Arithmetic and passages: P-010, P-012, P-013; covering rows R021, R026, R034.\n[Affected rows/fields] R022, R025, R035 (plus stated R034, R045); Summary balance\n[Consequence of changing it] Changing a base (e.g., fewer eligible signers) changes the residual counts and the inferred share of the per-stage balance; re-labelling the two eliminees as a different cohort changes the count of stated outcomes but not the total exits.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q5\n[Review topic] Anonymous identities and mappings (combining bidders; types)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: the two bidders that combined as Bidder 3 were two of the four finalists - necessarily the $80.00-$85.00 submitter (R019) and the third, otherwise unnamed, submitter initially at or above $80.00 - because the four advancing units are the Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and those two, and both combining members were invited to the final round. The ledger keeps the combination anonymous (R026), treats Unnamed financial bidder 1's exit as a Count-0 identity row (R035, recommended reading: inside Bidder 3), and does not move counts to a name. Types: Financial for both finalists and for Bidder 2/Bidder 3 by the cohort inference (Q3).\n[Why and source] Advancement arithmetic P-013 (four bidders at or above $80.00 = three initially at or above $80.00 per P-012 plus Bidder 2 after its raise) and the three December bidding units (P-020); combination facts P-014. The filing never identifies the members, so identity stays a hypothesis. Alternative: one combiner was not an invitee - rejected because the fourth finalist would then be unaccounted for among the December bidders.\n[Affected rows/fields] R019, R021, R024, R025, R026, R034, R035; Summary participants\n[Consequence of changing it] If a reviewer accepts a different mapping, R035's recommended reading changes but no count or balance changes (Count 0); if a combiner was not a finalist, the R2/R3 unit counts and R025's residual basis would need restating.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q6\n[Review topic] Formality and Conditions levels (borderline assessments)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: IOI rows (R018-R023, R021 cohort) Informal with Conditions 'Insufficient evidence' - preliminary non-binding indications after October diligence access, no formal signal and no stated financing/diligence condition; not Heavy by context because each bidder had substantive data-room and management access before indicating. Final-bid rows (R031, R032) and best-and-final rows (R038, R039) Formal (bidder-returned acquisition agreement/transaction documents; price confirmation for Bidder 2) with Light conditions (committed financing documented or confirmed; remaining matters were final documentation, as the 12/13 board approval was subject to resolving open points). Bidder 3's 12/10 communication is a Valuation statement, not a bid: per-share cells are blank and the value stays in text (R033). No LOIs, no 'None' levels, no late-reconfirmation rows, and the winner does have Formal rows.\n[Why and source] Signals in P-020, P-022, P-023; conditions facts in P-016, P-017, P-024; the instruction's formality signals and conditions tests (diligence-access context for preliminary indications; 'None' requires affirmative readiness). The 12/12 'substantially executable' formulation supports Light rather than None.\n[Affected rows/fields] R018-R023, R031-R039\n[Consequence of changing it] Reclassifying IOIs as Formal or Heavy would change the conditionality record but not counts; treating the valuation statement as a bid would create a bound price observation and a second bid row for Bidder 3; classifying the finals as 'None' would overstate readiness given the open points resolved only at signing.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q7\n[Review topic] Working dates and display order conventions\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: NDA wave Working date 10/04/2014 (midpoint of 10/01-10/07) with the interval preserved; 27-contact Working date 09/22/2014 (midpoint of mid-August-end October); R3 and the projection-update rows 11/15/2014 (November midpoints); Bidder 3 formation 11/03/2014 (Assigned: bound - after the 11/03 meeting, day not disclosed); inferred closings use the deadline/decision day (10/30, 11/03, 12/10). Same-day blocks (10/30 deadline vs submissions; 12/10 bids, valuation, non-submission and revision; 12/14 signing, announcement, rollover resolution and Bidder 2's outcome) use a deterministic display order; the relative order within them is not established by the filing and the shared dates are a display convention. A reviewer may adopt the alternative first-day reading for the NDA wave (10/01) and the 10/30/2014 bound for the contact row.\n[Why and source] Instruction's date rules; intervals and relative expressions in P-008, P-010, P-014, P-015, P-021, P-022, P-023, P-025. Bounds are tightened where a later passage shows the event (e.g., the 11/03 board had the IOI set before it, so all submissions sit at 10/30).\n[Affected rows/fields] R011, R012, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\n[Consequence of changing it] Moving the NDA wave to 10/01 would place it before the 10/03 board update and might suggest NDAs preceded that update; moving R3's Working date later narrows the gap to the 12/04-05 revision but changes no facts. Any reassignment must keep Working dates non-decreasing and inside each row's own bounds.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q8\n[Review topic] Comparability, consideration and other-scope coverage\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: no other-scope bids (nothing to exclude from core counts); single currency USD; the only non-cash element is Longview's rollover of 3,012,050 shares into Parent equity, treated as support rather than a bidding-group membership change or a partial-company offer; equity value is a labelled calculation (99,455,151 x $83.00 = about $8.25 billion), not a filing-stated total; market references ($77.67 close on 12/12/2014; 38.8% premium to 07/02/2014; about $78.00 reference on 12/10) are benchmarks, not offers; funding inputs (debt up to $6.95 billion, equity up to about $1.83 billion, rollover $250 million, ~$425 million cash) are as disclosed.\n[Why and source] P-001, P-011, P-022, X-007 (premium), X-008, X-017, X-019, X-020, X-026, X-029; instruction rules on per-share cells, rollover support and labelled conversions.\n[Affected rows/fields] R019, R033, R035, R038, R040, R044, R045; Summary deal facts and inputs\n[Consequence of changing it] Re-normalizing the rollover or adding net debt would be a new labelled calculation, not an observed price; treating the rollover as a membership change would alter the R040/R044 treatment and the unit-count narrative; treating the equity value as filing-stated would misstate its provenance.\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q1\n[Review topic] Process and round map; R1 anchor and finality values\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: one process (2014 sale process); R1 anchored on the first-week-of-October confidentiality wave (R015), not the 08/13 decision, 08/19 announcement or 10/03 board update (all retained as rows R008/R009/R013 so the boundary can move). R2 opens with the 11/03 advancement (Inferred final); R3 opens with the November request for 'final bids' (Announced as final); the 12/04-05 and 12/10-12 events are deadline revisions inside R3, not new rounds. Keep R1 'Not final' (preliminary IOI stage).\n[Why and source] The instruction prefers the first target-organized admission step when no dated first outreach wave exists; the filing reports contacts coming to J.P. Morgan ('J.P. Morgan was contacted by 27 potential participants', P-008) and dates the CA wave (P-010). The first final-offer request opens a round even with the same bidders (P-015; initial 12/05 date in P-016); the later improvement request is a deadline revision, not a round (P-021). Alternatives: anchor R1 at the 08/13 decision or 08/19 announcement; open R3 at the 12/10 deadline instead of the November request; merge R2 into R3.\n[Affected rows/fields] R014, R015, R016, R024, R026, R027, R029, R036; Summary process/round map\n[Consequence of changing it] Moving the R1 anchor changes the round-1 scope (e.g., an 08/13 anchor would pull pre-NDA contacts into R1). A separate final-solicitation round raised at 12/10 instead of November would shift the deadline history between rounds; merging R2/R3 would drop the advancement/Documentation transition, and the round-bidder tallies (6 IOI units; 4 advancing; 2 written finals) would need restating.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q2\n[Review topic] Deadline history and treatments\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: 10/30/2014 IOI date - Enforced (R017; board advanced on 11/03 without revision). 12/05/2014 final-bid date - Extended; superseded on 12/04-05 before arrival, so it gets no milestone row and is recorded on the Deadline revised row R029. 12/10/2014 - Extended (R030; moved to 12/12 by R036). 12/12/2014 - Enforced (R037; best-and-final bids received and the board acted on 12/13). No deadline was 'Late bids accepted': Bidder 3's verbal valuation was received on the 12/10 date itself, and it then submitted nothing rather than a late bid.\n[Why and source] Dates and sequence in P-011, P-012, P-013, P-016, P-020, P-021, P-023, P-024. The instruction treats a post-deadline request for improved bids by a new date as a Deadline revised (extension), and a date superseded before arrival needs no milestone row. The 12/05 date was set but never reached; its replacement was decided 12/04-05.\n[Affected rows/fields] R017, R022, R029, R030, R036, R037; Summary deadline map\n[Consequence of changing it] If the 12/05 date were treated as reached (not superseded), it would need its own Deadline row/Enforced value; if the 12/10 improvement request were treated as a fresh Deadline set or new round, the R3 boundary and tallies change.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q3\n[Review topic] Count and population bases (conflicts and residuals)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended readings: (a) six IOI submitters (background, p.24) over '5 bidder groups' (Reasons, p.27) - the background is specific and contemporaneous, and the six include the two below-$80 submitters; (b) all 15 NDA signers were eligible for the 10/30 solicitation (they had been told the due date), so the residual is 9 non-submitters (R022); (c) the two eliminees are the two residual submitters within R021 whose indications were below $80.00 - a count-based residual, not named identities; (d) 27 contacts (p.23) with the 'more than 25' wording (p.27) treated as a consistent lower bound; (e) Bidder 2, Bidder 3 and Unnamed financial bidder 1 are typed Financial by inference from the all-financial 15-signer cohort - the filing never states their type individually.\n[Why and source] Counts at P-008, P-010, P-012, P-013, P-014; conflict passages P-012 vs X-008; type basis P-010 ('15 potentially interested financial buyers'). The instruction requires residual cohorts to be disjoint from individually recorded members and counts to be scoped, with bases surfaced where uncertain.\n[Affected rows/fields] R011, R012, R015, R018-R021, R023, R024, R025; Summary counts block\n[Consequence of changing it] If some signers were not eligible for the IOI solicitation, the 9-non-submitter residual shrinks; if '5 groups' were preferred, the round-1 tally falls by one (the six otherwise reconcile to 4 advancing + 2 eliminated). Any change to the R021/R025 split changes the inferred-elimination count.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q4\n[Review topic] Every inferred closing row (grouped by transition)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: (a) 10/30/2014 - 9 unnamed NDA signers Did not submit, Inferred: residual (15 NDA signers - 6 submitters), Count 9, Decided by Unknown, reason Not stated (R022); (b) 11/03/2014 - 2 unnamed submitters Dropped by target, Inferred: residual (6 submitters - 4 advancing), Count 2, Decided by Target, Exit reason Not stated (the lower-price context is preserved in Terms; R025); (c) by 12/10/2014 - Unnamed financial bidder 1, Count-0 identity row (recommended reading: closed inside Bidder 3; R035). Stated comparators: Bidder 3 Did not submit (R034) and Bidder 2 Not selected at signing (R045). No identities, motives or permanent withdrawals are inferred.\n[Why and source] Instruction's closing rules: residual non-submissions by subtraction; eliminations by residual at the advancement; a named-but-silent party gets a Count-0 identity row naming the covering cohort; stated outcomes take no opener. Arithmetic and passages: P-010, P-012, P-013; covering rows R021, R026, R034.\n[Affected rows/fields] R022, R025, R035 (plus stated R034, R045); Summary balance\n[Consequence of changing it] Changing a base (e.g., fewer eligible signers) changes the residual counts and the inferred share of the per-stage balance; re-labelling the two eliminees as a different cohort changes the count of stated outcomes but not the total exits.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q5\n[Review topic] Anonymous identities and mappings (combining bidders; types)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: the two bidders that combined as Bidder 3 were two of the four finalists - necessarily the $80.00-$85.00 submitter (R019) and the third, otherwise unnamed, submitter initially at or above $80.00 - because the four advancing units are the Buyer Group, Bidder 2 and those two, and both combining members were invited to the final round. The ledger keeps the combination anonymous (R026), treats Unnamed financial bidder 1's exit as a Count-0 identity row (R035, recommended reading: inside Bidder 3), and does not move counts to a name. Types: Financial for both finalists and for Bidder 2/Bidder 3 by the cohort inference (Q3).\n[Why and source] Advancement arithmetic P-013 (four bidders at or above $80.00 = three initially at or above $80.00 per P-012 plus Bidder 2 after its raise) and the three December bidding units (P-020); combination facts P-014. The filing never identifies the members, so identity stays a hypothesis. Alternative: one combiner was not an invitee - rejected because the fourth finalist would then be unaccounted for among the December bidders.\n[Affected rows/fields] R019, R021, R024, R025, R026, R034, R035; Summary participants\n[Consequence of changing it] If a reviewer accepts a different mapping, R035's recommended reading changes but no count or balance changes (Count 0); if a combiner was not a finalist, the R2/R3 unit counts and R025's residual basis would need restating.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q6\n[Review topic] Formality and Conditions levels (borderline assessments)\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: IOI rows (R018-R023, R021 cohort) Informal with Conditions 'Insufficient evidence' - preliminary non-binding indications after October diligence access, no formal signal and no stated financing/diligence condition; not Heavy by context because each bidder had substantive data-room and management access before indicating. Final-bid rows (R031, R032) and best-and-final rows (R038, R039) Formal (bidder-returned acquisition agreement/transaction documents; price confirmation for Bidder 2) with Light conditions (committed financing documented or confirmed; remaining matters were final documentation, as the 12/13 board approval was subject to resolving open points). Bidder 3's 12/10 communication is a Valuation statement, not a bid: per-share cells are blank and the value stays in text (R033). No LOIs, no 'None' levels, no late-reconfirmation rows, and the winner does have Formal rows.\n[Why and source] Signals in P-020, P-022, P-023; conditions facts in P-016, P-017, P-024; the instruction's formality signals and conditions tests (diligence-access context for preliminary indications; 'None' requires affirmative readiness). The 12/12 'substantially executable' formulation supports Light rather than None.\n[Affected rows/fields] R018-R023, R031-R039\n[Consequence of changing it] Reclassifying IOIs as Formal or Heavy would change the conditionality record but not counts; treating the valuation statement as a bid would create a bound price observation and a second bid row for Bidder 3; classifying the finals as 'None' would overstate readiness given the open points resolved only at signing.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q7\n[Review topic] Working dates and display order conventions\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: NDA wave Working date 10/04/2014 (midpoint of 10/01-10/07) with the interval preserved; 27-contact Working date 09/22/2014 (midpoint of mid-August-end October); R3 and the projection-update rows 11/15/2014 (November midpoints); Bidder 3 formation 11/03/2014 (Assigned: bound - after the 11/03 meeting, day not disclosed); inferred closings use the deadline/decision day (10/30, 11/03, 12/10). Same-day blocks (10/30 deadline vs submissions; 12/10 bids, valuation, non-submission and revision; 12/14 signing, announcement, rollover resolution and Bidder 2's outcome) use a deterministic display order; the relative order within them is not established by the filing and the shared dates are a display convention. A reviewer may adopt the alternative first-day reading for the NDA wave (10/01) and the 10/30/2014 bound for the contact row.\n[Why and source] Instruction's date rules; intervals and relative expressions in P-008, P-010, P-014, P-015, P-021, P-022, P-023, P-025. Bounds are tightened where a later passage shows the event (e.g., the 11/03 board had the IOI set before it, so all submissions sit at 10/30).\n[Affected rows/fields] R011, R012, R014, R015, R022, R023, R026, R027, R028, R035; Date fields\n[Consequence of changing it] Moving the NDA wave to 10/01 would place it before the 10/03 board update and might suggest NDAs preceded that update; moving R3's Working date later narrows the gap to the 12/04-05 revision but changes no facts. Any reassignment must keep Working dates non-decreasing and inside each row's own bounds.\n====================================================================================================\n[Q] Q8\n[Review topic] Comparability, consideration and other-scope coverage\n[Recommended answer] Recommended: no other-scope bids (nothing to exclude from core counts); single currency USD; the only non-cash element is Longview's rollover of 3,012,050 shares into Parent equity, treated as support rather than a bidding-group membership change or a partial-company offer; equity value is a labelled calculation (99,455,151 x $83.00 = about $8.25 billion), not a filing-stated total; market references ($77.67 close on 12/12/2014; 38.8% premium to 07/02/2014; about $78.00 reference on 12/10) are benchmarks, not offers; funding inputs (debt up to $6.95 billion, equity up to about $1.83 billion, rollover $250 million, ~$425 million cash) are as disclosed.\n[Why and source] P-001, P-011, P-022, X-007 (premium), X-008, X-017, X-019, X-020, X-026, X-029; instruction rules on per-share cells, rollover support and labelled conversions.\n[Affected rows/fields] R019, R033, R035, R038, R040, R044, R045; Summary deal facts and inputs\n[Consequence of changing it] Re-normalizing the rollover or adding net debt would be a new labelled calculation, not an observed price; treating the rollover as a membership change would alter the R040/R044 treatment and the unit-count narrative; treating the equity value as filing-stated would misstate its provenance.\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Command exited with code 0."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /tmp/opencode/petsmart && python3 - <<'EOF'\\nfrom openpyxl import load_workbook\\nwb = load_workbook('/home/uctpiaj/work/extraction/petsmart.xlsx')\\nwq = wb['Questions']\\nfor r in range(2, wq.max_row+1):\\n    print('='*100)\\n    for c in range(1, 7):\\n        v = wq.cell(row=r, column=c).value\\n        if v: print(f\\\"[{wq.cell(row=1,column=c).value}] {v}\\\")\\nEOF\"}"},"time":{"start":1789825253360,"end":1789825253911}}}}
